msgid "**API access:** the deploy reads the API token Weblate issued for its administrator and persists it in the token store, where the gateway reads it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**API bot roles of the Infinito.Nexus inventory.** `services.erpnext.api_bot.extra_roles` there holds the union of the consumers' needs: store `System Manager`, `Provisioning Bot`, `Sales Master Manager`, `Sales Manager`, `Sales User`, `Item Manager`, `Stock Manager`, `Accounts User`; security check the roles its provisioning needs on the bot. Other tenants keep the empty default."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Access Locks**: a role-gated application (``services.sso.oauth2.allowed_groups``) shows a lock on its tile when the signed-in user holds none of its groups; the lock links to ``web-svc-access-request`` when that service is deployed, and asks an anonymous visitor to sign in. The tile always stays clickable, the SSO gate decides. Switch the locks off with ``services.dashboard.locks.enabled: false``."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Access Locks**: a role-gated application (`services.sso.oauth2.allowed_groups`) shows a lock on its tile when the signed-in user holds none of its groups; the lock links to `web-svc-access-request` when that service is deployed, and asks an anonymous visitor to sign in. The tile always stays clickable, the SSO gate decides. Switch the locks off with `services.dashboard.locks.enabled: false`."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Access is entity-scoped and read-mostly by default.** Only entities explicitly exposed to the Assist API are reachable via MCP. Mutating/actuating tools (locks, covers, switches) are off by default and require operator opt-in, per 050's mutating-tools rule."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Access log class:** the reverse proxy writes its access log to stdout and its error log to stderr, and Docker's journald driver stores a container's stdout lines at journal priority 6 and its stderr lines at priority 3. A line of an application in `LOG_COLLECTOR_ACCESS_LOG_APPLICATIONS` (`svc-prx-openresty`) at priority 6 is therefore classed `access`, while the proxy's error log stays `application`. The critical-line alerts of Loki and Grafana select `log_class=\"application\"` only, so an access log line no longer raises them. The proxy's error log still does: a request it logs as an error, such as a missing file under the CDN location (`open() \"<path>\" failed`), carries the request path into an `application` line, and an alert word in that path raises both alerts."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Access log class:** the reverse proxy writes its access log to stdout and its error log to stderr, and Docker’s journald driver stores a container’s stdout lines at journal priority 6 and its stderr lines at priority 3. A line of an application in ``LOG_COLLECTOR_ACCESS_LOG_APPLICATIONS`` (``svc-prx-openresty``) at priority 6 is therefore classed ``access``, while the proxy’s error log stays ``application``. The critical-line alerts of Loki and Grafana select ``log_class=\"application\"`` only, so an access log line no longer raises them. The proxy’s error log still does: a request it logs as an error, such as a missing file under the CDN location (``open() \"<path>\" failed``), carries the request path into an ``application`` line, and an alert word in that path raises both alerts."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Access the Application Container:** First, gain shell access to the Pixelfed application container. Use the command provided in the README:"
msgstr "**आवेदन कंटेनर का उपयोग करें:** सबसे पहले, शेल एक्सेस प्राप्त करें Pixelfed आवेदन कंटेनर README में दिए गए आदेश का उपयोग करें:"

msgid "**Access through native OIDC.** Grafana signs in through Keycloak with `auth.generic_oauth`. The role group `administrator` maps to the Grafana Admin role and a new role group `auditor` maps to Viewer; every other account is refused. A local admin exists only as break-glass access."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Account adoption:** `$wgOpenIDConnect_MigrateUsersByUserName` links the first OIDC login to the local account of the same name, so the platform administrator keeps the account `createAndPromote` provisioned."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Account adoption:** ``$wgOpenIDConnect_MigrateUsersByUserName`` links the first OIDC login to the local account of the same name, so the platform administrator keeps the account ``createAndPromote`` provisioned."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Account linking by name only:** [oauth2/account-linking-by-name.patch](./files/patch/oauth2/account-linking-by-name.patch) removes the primary-email step of `ACCOUNT_LINKING=auto`, so an SSO sign-in links only to the account whose name equals its `preferred_username`; a collision on email alone is refused on the sign-in page."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Account linking by name only:** `oauth2/account-linking-by-name.patch <./files/patch/oauth2/account-linking-by-name.patch>`__ removes the primary-email step of ``ACCOUNT_LINKING=auto``, so an SSO sign-in links only to the account whose name equals its ``preferred_username``; a collision on email alone is refused on the sign-in page."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Accounting & Finance:** Handle invoicing, payments, bank reconciliation, and financial reporting. Supports multi-currency and multi-company operations."
msgstr "**लेखा और वित्त:** चालान, भुगतान, बैंक मिलान और वित्तीय रिपोर्टिंग को संभाल लें। बहु-मुद्रा और बहु-कंपनी संचालन का समर्थन करता है।"

msgid "**Accounts, app passwords and forwards are provisioned in batches.** Each phase (create, password update, app password list, mint, retire, drop, forward script list, read, upload, activate) is one JMAP request for all accounts. A phase on the bots' app passwords or the forward scripts carries one method call per account, addressed through its `accountId` by the recovery admin, at most `STALWART_JMAP_MAX_METHOD_CALLS` (Stalwart's default `maxMethodCalls`) per request, and a refusal names the account it hit."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Accounts, app passwords and forwards are provisioned in batches.** Each phase (create, password update, app password list, mint, retire, drop, forward script list, read, upload, activate) is one JMAP request for all accounts. A phase on the bots’ app passwords or the forward scripts carries one method call per account, addressed through its ``accountId`` by the recovery admin, at most ``STALWART_JMAP_MAX_METHOD_CALLS`` (Stalwart’s default ``maxMethodCalls``) per request, and a refusal names the account it hit."
