# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Assignment is deterministic, never random.** It follows the row's index in the global discovery order and the sweep number, so re-running a sweep reproduces the run. Discovery order itself is stabilised by `INFINITO_DISCOVERY_SEED`, which CI sets to the run id, so the plan table, the discover job and every chunk block of one run agree without passing state between them."
msgstr "**असाइनमेंट निश्चित है, कभी यादृच्छिक नहीं है।** यह वैश्विक खोज आदेश और स्वीप संख्या में पंक्ति के सूचकांक का अनुसरण करता है, इसलिए एक स्वीप फिर से चलाने से रन को पुन: उत्पन्न होता है। डिस्कवरी ऑर्डर स्वयं ही स्थिर है `INFINITO_DISCOVERY_SEED`, जो सीआई रन आईडी के लिए सेट करता है, इसलिए योजना तालिका, खोज कार्य और एक रन के हर हिस्से के ब्लॉक उनके बीच राज्य पारित किए बिना सहमत होते हैं।"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Assignment reads the row's position like an odometer.** The distro is the low digit and the filesystem the high one, so consecutive rows walk every pairing instead of a diagonal through it. Turning both on the position directly covers only `n` of the `n x m` pairs whenever the two pools are the same length, and the sweep number does not unlock it, because it shifts both by the same amount."
msgstr "**असाइनमेंट ने पंक्ति की स्थिति को ओडोमीटर की तरह पढ़ा।** डिस्ट्रो निम्न अंक है और फ़ाइल सिस्टम उच्च एक है, इसलिए लगातार पंक्तियां इसके माध्यम से एक विकर्ण के बजाय हर जोड़ी जाती हैं। स्थिति पर दोनों को सीधे ही कवर करना `n` का `n x m` जब भी दो पूल समान लंबाई होते हैं, और स्वीप संख्या इसे अनलॉक नहीं करती है, क्योंकि यह उसी राशि दोनों को बदल देता है।"

msgid "**Associated Groups:** The OIDC ``groups`` claim becomes the user’s associated groups, so a Discourse group can add the members of a Keycloak role group automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Associated Groups:** The OIDC `groups` claim becomes the user's associated groups, so a Discourse group can add the members of a Keycloak role group automatically."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Atomic:** A fragment is applied in a single ``nft -f`` transaction, so the table is never observed half built."
msgstr "**परमाणु:** एक टुकड़ा एक एकल में लागू होता है ``nft -f`` लेन-देन, इसलिए तालिका को कभी भी आधा बनाया नहीं जाता है।"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Atomic:** A fragment is applied in a single `nft -f` transaction, so the table is never observed half built."
msgstr "**परमाणु:** एक टुकड़ा एक एकल में लागू होता है `nft -f` लेन-देन, इसलिए तालिका को कभी भी आधा बनाया नहीं जाता है।"

msgid "**Audit ingest:** A throwaway instance spools audit entries locally and sends them with its own sequence numbers; the live provisioner assigns time, sequence and a hash-chained link (``utils.orchestrator.audit``), reports gaps in the spooled sequence, and keeps the chain insert-only so a later edit or deletion is detectable."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Audit ingest:** A throwaway instance spools audit entries locally and sends them with its own sequence numbers; the live provisioner assigns time, sequence and a hash-chained link (`utils.orchestrator.audit`), reports gaps in the spooled sequence, and keeps the chain insert-only so a later edit or deletion is detectable."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Audit trail:** A ``file`` audit device at ``stdout/``, declared in the server config, writes every request, with the accessing identity and a timestamp, to the server’s stdout and so to the container log. Secret values appear only as salted HMACs. Every deploy reads a probe secret and fails unless the log shows that read with its identity and time."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Audit trail:** A `file` audit device at `stdout/`, declared in the server config, writes every request, with the accessing identity and a timestamp, to the server's stdout and so to the container log. Secret values appear only as salted HMACs. Every deploy reads a probe secret and fails unless the log shows that read with its identity and time."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Audit:** the realm records admin events, so every membership the service grants appears under the approver who confirmed it, for as many days as ``services.keycloak.events.admin.expiration_days`` of `web-app-keycloak <../web-app-keycloak/README.md>`__ sets."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Audit:** the realm records admin events, so every membership the service grants appears under the approver who confirmed it, for as many days as `services.keycloak.events.admin.expiration_days` of [web-app-keycloak](../web-app-keycloak/README.md) sets."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Auth caveat is documented.** Home Assistant uses its own auth (users + long-lived tokens + `trusted_proxies`), not full OIDC. The MCP endpoint is authenticated with a Home Assistant credential stored in `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:`; if platform SSO in front of the HA UI is wanted, the trusted-proxy header approach and its limits MUST be documented in the role README."
msgstr "**Auth craat दस्तावेज है।** होम असिस्टेंट अपने स्वयं के auth का उपयोग करता है (उपयोगकर्ता + लंबे समय तक चलने वाले टोकन + `trusted_proxies`), पूर्ण ओआईडीसी नहीं MCP समापन बिंदु एक साथ प्रमाणित है Home Assistant में संग्रहीत क्रेडेंशियल `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:`; यदि एचए यूआई के सामने एसएसओ मंच चाहता है, तो विश्वसनीय-प्रोक्सी हेडर दृष्टिकोण और इसकी सीमा MUST को भूमिका README में प्रलेखित किया जाएगा।."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Auth:** \"Sign in with Bluesky\" — AT Protocol OAuth against the user's PDS / identity. No local password store."
msgstr "**प्रमाणन:** \"साइन इन करें Bluesky\" - उपयोगकर्ता के पीडीएस / पहचान के खिलाफ AT प्रोटोकॉल OAuth। कोई स्थानीय पासवर्ड स्टोर नहीं है।."

msgid "**Authenticated push:** ``loki.write`` sends to ``https://loki.<DOMAIN_PRIMARY>/loki/api/v1/push`` with the ``push_token`` of ``web-svc-loki`` as bearer token, read from the ``0600`` env file, and with the tenant header ``X-Scope-OrgID``. Pushes retry with backoff (``services.svc-log-collector.push``) while Loki is not reachable."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Authenticated push:** `loki.write` sends to `https://loki.<DOMAIN_PRIMARY>/loki/api/v1/push` with the `push_token` of `web-svc-loki` as bearer token, read from the `0600` env file, and with the tenant header `X-Scope-OrgID`. Pushes retry with backoff (`services.svc-log-collector.push`) while Loki is not reachable."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Authorization subject.** MCP integrations prefer user-scoped authorization. Service-account or administrator-scoped MCP credentials are allowed only for read-only default tool sets, or when the role README documents the upstream limitation and the operator explicitly enables mutating tools."
msgstr "**प्राधिकरण विषय।** MCP एकीकरण उपयोगकर्ता-coped प्राधिकरण पसंद करते हैं। सेवा-खाता या प्रशासक-coped MCP क्रेडेंशियल को केवल पढ़ने-केवल डिफ़ॉल्ट टूल सेट के लिए अनुमति दी जाती है, या जब भूमिका README अपस्ट्रीम सीमा को दस्तावेज करता है और ऑपरेटर स्पष्ट रूप से उत्परिवर्तन उपकरण को सक्षम बनाता है।"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Auto-Discovery**: Scans your NGINX ``servers`` directory for ``.conf`` files. 🔍"
msgstr "**ऑटो डिस्कवरी**: अपने NGINX स्कैन करें ``servers`` निर्देशिका ``.conf`` फ़ाइलें 🔍"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Auto-Discovery**: Scans your NGINX `servers` directory for `.conf` files. 🔍"
msgstr "**ऑटो डिस्कवरी**: अपने NGINX स्कैन करें `servers` निर्देशिका `.conf` फ़ाइलें 🔍"

msgid "**Auto-created accounts** reach `User::save()` through SuiteCRM's own `CreateUser` while the request is still anonymous. Since 8.10.2 that save answers `RuntimeException: Not authorized` and forces `status = Inactive`, so `files/patch/external-auth-user-create.patch` makes the stored system user the current user around the save and restores the caller's afterwards. [`files/Dockerfile`](./files/Dockerfile) applies it with `patch -F0` on the unpacked release; the image build fails once the hunk stops matching."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Auto-created accounts** reach ``User::save()`` through SuiteCRM’s own ``CreateUser`` while the request is still anonymous. Since 8.10.2 that save answers ``RuntimeException: Not authorized`` and forces ``status = Inactive``, so ``files/patch/external-auth-user-create.patch`` makes the stored system user the current user around the save and restores the caller’s afterwards. ```files/Dockerfile`` <./files/Dockerfile>`__ applies it with ``patch -F0`` on the unpacked release; the image build fails once the hunk stops matching."
msgstr ""

