# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Preloaded models:** Every entry of ``services.lmstudio.preload_models`` is downloaded on the hosting node with ``lms get --gguf``, overlapped and reaped like the Ollama pre-pull. Each entry carries the ``source`` repository to download, the ``quant`` variant to take from it, the ``name`` LM Studio indexes that repository under and the gateway addresses it by, and the ``alias`` the gateway publishes it as. ``source`` is a full Hugging Face URL, never a search term: a search term resolves to whichever model the catalogue lists first. ``quant`` is appended as ``@<variant>`` and is required: without it LM Studio picks the variant itself, and the ``file``, ``sha256`` and ``bytes`` the entry declares then describe a guess that the store check and the download budget are both measured against."
msgstr "**प्रीलोडेड मॉडल:** प्रत्येक प्रविष्टि ``services.lmstudio.preload_models`` होस्टिंग नोड पर डाउनलोड किया गया है ``lms get --gguf``, overlapped और reaped की तरह Ollama पूर्व पुल। प्रत्येक प्रविष्टि होती है ``source`` डाउनलोड करने के लिए भंडार, ``quant`` इसे लेने के लिए वेरिएंट, ``name`` LM Studio अनुक्रमणिका जो नीचे पीछे छोड़ते हैं और प्रवेश द्वार उसे संबोधित करते हैं, और ``alias`` प्रवेश द्वार इसे प्रकाशित करता है। ``source`` एक पूर्ण Hugging फेस URL है, कभी एक खोज शब्द नहीं: एक खोज शब्द का संकल्प करता है जो भी कैटलॉग को पहले सूचीबद्ध करता है। ``quant`` जैसा ``@<variant>`` और आवश्यक है: इसके बिना LM Studio वेरिएंट को खुद चुनिए और वेरिएंट को खुद चुनिए, और ``file``, ``sha256`` और ``bytes`` प्रविष्टि घोषणा करती है कि तब यह अनुमान लगाया जाता है कि स्टोर चेक और डाउनलोड बजट दोनों के खिलाफ मापा जाता है।."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Preloaded models:** Every entry of `services.lmstudio.preload_models` is downloaded on the hosting node with `lms get --gguf`, overlapped and reaped like the Ollama pre-pull. Each entry carries the `source` repository to download, the `quant` variant to take from it, the `name` LM Studio indexes that repository under and the gateway addresses it by, and the `alias` the gateway publishes it as. `source` is a full Hugging Face URL, never a search term: a search term resolves to whichever model the catalogue lists first. `quant` is appended as `@<variant>` and is required: without it LM Studio picks the variant itself, and the `file`, `sha256` and `bytes` the entry declares then describe a guess that the store check and the download budget are both measured against."
