msgstr "बेसरो OSS बैकेंड में एक मूल MCP सर्वर को जहाज करता है, जिसे Django से पहले ASGI रूट पर लगाया जाता है। ग्राहक इसे नहीं पहुंचते। भूमिका इसे चलाता है *अपस्ट्रीम* a [`svc-ai-mcp-adapter`](../svc-ai-mcp-adapter/README.md) साइडकार (`classification: adapter_server`), और साइडकार एकमात्र MCP सतह है जो उपभोक्ता को दिया जाता है।"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Baserow ships a native MCP server in the OSS backend, mounted on the ASGI root ahead of Django. Clients do not reach it. The role runs it as the *upstream* of a ```svc-ai-mcp-adapter`` <../svc-ai-mcp-adapter/README.md>`__ sidecar (``classification: adapter_server``), and the sidecar is the only MCP surface a consumer is given."
msgstr "बेसरो OSS बैकेंड में एक मूल MCP सर्वर को जहाज करता है, जिसे Django से पहले ASGI रूट पर लगाया जाता है। ग्राहक इसे नहीं पहुंचते। भूमिका इसे चलाता है *अपस्ट्रीम* a ```svc-ai-mcp-adapter`` <../svc-ai-mcp-adapter/README.md>`__ sidecar (``classification: adapter_server``), और साइडकार एकमात्र MCP सतह है जो उपभोक्ता को दिया जाता है।"

msgid "Baserow's Caddy layer answers only the hosts named in `BASEROW_PUBLIC_URL` and `BASEROW_EXTRA_PUBLIC_URLS`; any other host is treated as a published builder domain and gets `404`. The role lists every network sibling of the canonical URL in `BASEROW_EXTRA_PUBLIC_URLS`, so the onion vhost's `/healthz/ready` probe still reaches the backend."
msgstr ""

msgid "Baserow's native `openid_connect` auth provider belongs to the bundled enterprise plugin and refuses to register without a paid Baserow Enterprise licence, so the addon ships declared and off and the oauth2-proxy front door above stays the supported SSO path. An operator holding that licence switches the addon on; [files/playwright/addons/openid_connect.spec.js](./files/playwright/addons/openid_connect.spec.js) then asserts the provider is registered and offered on the login page."
msgstr ""

msgid "Baserow's web frontend sends every API call to its one `PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL` and marks its `jwt_token` cookie `Secure` from its one public URL, so a session cannot live on the onion sibling. `meta/networks.yml` therefore opts into `reachability.handover`: the onion vhost in [proxy.conf.j2](templates/proxy.conf.j2) answers `/` with a redirect to the same path on the canonical clearnet URL."
msgstr ""

msgid "Baserow’s Caddy layer answers only the hosts named in ``BASEROW_PUBLIC_URL`` and ``BASEROW_EXTRA_PUBLIC_URLS``; any other host is treated as a published builder domain and gets ``404``. The role lists every network sibling of the canonical URL in ``BASEROW_EXTRA_PUBLIC_URLS``, so the onion vhost’s ``/healthz/ready`` probe still reaches the backend."
msgstr ""

msgid "Baserow’s native ``openid_connect`` auth provider belongs to the bundled enterprise plugin and refuses to register without a paid Baserow Enterprise licence, so the addon ships declared and off and the oauth2-proxy front door above stays the supported SSO path. An operator holding that licence switches the addon on; `files/playwright/addons/openid_connect.spec.js <./files/playwright/addons/openid_connect.spec.js>`__ then asserts the provider is registered and offered on the login page."
msgstr ""

msgid "Baserow’s web frontend sends every API call to its one ``PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL`` and marks its ``jwt_token`` cookie ``Secure`` from its one public URL, so a session cannot live on the onion sibling. ``meta/networks.yml`` therefore opts into ``reachability.handover``: the onion vhost in `proxy.conf.j2 <templates/proxy.conf.j2>`__ answers ``/`` with a redirect to the same path on the canonical clearnet URL."
msgstr ""

