msgid "Per-consumer S3 identities are rendered into ``s3.json``: each consuming role receives an access key and bucket-scoped ``Read``, ``Write``, ``WriteAcp``, ``List``, and ``Tagging`` actions, and consumers marked ``public`` additionally receive anonymous read on their bucket. Consumer buckets are created through ``weed shell`` when a consumer role requests provisioning."
msgstr ""

msgid "Per-consumer S3 identities are rendered into ``s3.json``: each consuming role receives an access key and bucket-scoped ``Read``, ``Write``, ``WriteAcp``, ``List``, and ``Tagging`` actions, and consumers marked ``public`` additionally receive anonymous read on their bucket. Consumer buckets are created through ``weed shell`` when a consumer role requests provisioning. The bucket of every consumer not marked ``public`` carries a bucket policy statement ``DenyAnonymousRead`` that denies all unsigned reads, so a ``public-read`` ACL set by an app never exposes an object; signed and presigned requests are unaffected. Every deploy of this role converges that statement on all existing consumer buckets, adding it to private buckets and removing it from public ones, and a consumer’s provisioning applies it right after creating the bucket. Other statements an operator adds to a consumer’s bucket policy are kept."
msgstr ""

msgid "Per-consumer S3 identities are rendered into `s3.json`: each consuming role receives an access key and bucket-scoped `Read`, `Write`, `WriteAcp`, `List`, and `Tagging` actions, and consumers marked `public` additionally receive anonymous read on their bucket. Consumer buckets are created through `weed shell` when a consumer role requests provisioning."
msgstr ""

msgid "Per-consumer S3 identities are rendered into `s3.json`: each consuming role receives an access key and bucket-scoped `Read`, `Write`, `WriteAcp`, `List`, and `Tagging` actions, and consumers marked `public` additionally receive anonymous read on their bucket. Consumer buckets are created through `weed shell` when a consumer role requests provisioning. The bucket of every consumer not marked `public` carries a bucket policy statement `DenyAnonymousRead` that denies all unsigned reads, so a `public-read` ACL set by an app never exposes an object; signed and presigned requests are unaffected. Every deploy of this role converges that statement on all existing consumer buckets, adding it to private buckets and removing it from public ones, and a consumer's provisioning applies it right after creating the bucket. Other statements an operator adds to a consumer's bucket policy are kept."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Per-consumer isolation"
msgstr "प्रति उपभोक्ता अलगाव"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Per-consumer provisioning (``tasks/01_init.yml``) runs with ``application_id=svc-db-rabbitmq`` and ``database_consumer_id=<consumer>``; it resolves the consumer’s vhost name, username and password via ``lookup('engine', 'rabbitmq', <consumer>, ...)`` and reconciles an idempotent vhost, user and ``set_permissions`` grant scoped to that vhost. Existing vhosts and users are skipped, and the consumer password is realigned with the inventory on every deploy."
msgstr "प्रति उपभोक्ता प्रावधान (``tasks/01_init.yml``) साथ ``application_id=svc-db-rabbitmq`` और ``database_consumer_id=<consumer>``; यह उपभोक्ता के भूत नाम, उपयोगकर्ता नाम और पासवर्ड के माध्यम से हल करता है ``lookup('engine', 'rabbitmq', <consumer>, ...)`` और एक idempotent भूत, उपयोगकर्ता और ``set_permissions`` उस भूत को दिया गया। मौजूदा भूत और उपयोगकर्ताओं को छोड़ दिया जाता है, और उपभोक्ता पासवर्ड प्रत्येक तैनाती पर सूची के साथ फिर से जुड़ा हुआ है।"

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Per-consumer provisioning (``tasks/01_init.yml``) runs with ``application_id=svc-db-redis`` and ``database_consumer_id=<consumer>``; it resolves the consumer’s username, password and key-prefix via ``lookup('engine', 'redis', <consumer>, ...)`` and reconciles an idempotent ``ACL SETUSER`` restricted to ``~{entity}:*``. The ACL users are recreated by the consumer’s ``01_init`` on every deploy, so a container restart that drops the in-memory ACL set is healed on the next run."
msgstr "प्रति उपभोक्ता प्रावधान (``tasks/01_init.yml``) साथ ``application_id=svc-db-redis`` और ``database_consumer_id=<consumer>``; यह उपभोक्ता के उपयोगकर्ता नाम, पासवर्ड और कुंजी-प्रीफिक्स के माध्यम से हल करता है ``lookup('engine', 'redis', <consumer>, ...)`` और idempotent ``ACL SETUSER`` तक सीमित ``~{entity}:*``. ACL उपयोगकर्ताओं को उपभोक्ता द्वारा पुनर्निर्मित किया जाता है ``01_init`` प्रत्येक तैनाती पर, इसलिए एक कंटेनर पुनरारंभ होता है जो इन-मेमोरी एसीएल सेट को अगले रन पर ठीक किया जाता है।"

