msgid "The role provisions new GitLab instances. Volumes, secrets and backups of a pre-CNG Omnibus deployment (`gitlab_config`, `gitlab_data`, `/etc/gitlab/gitlab-secrets.json`) are not migrated or restorable into the CNG layout; deploy against a fresh database and empty volumes."
msgstr "भूमिका नए प्रावधान GitLab उदाहरण एक पूर्व CNG Omnibus तैनाती की मात्रा, रहस्य और बैकअप (`gitlab_config`, `gitlab_data`, `/etc/gitlab/gitlab-secrets.json`) CNG लेआउट में माइग्रेट या बहाल नहीं हैं; एक ताजा डेटाबेस और खाली वॉल्यूम के खिलाफ तैनात।."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role publishes a public documentation site. [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml) pins `sso.enabled` and `sso.shared` to `false`, and the role ships no `meta/users.yml` and no account provisioning; [`templates/env.j2`](./templates/env.j2) only configures the build service. [`tasks/main.yml`](./tasks/main.yml) only wires the container and proxy stack and stages the Sphinx tooling into the build context. There is no account and no auth chain for the `biber` or `administrator` persona, so [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) declares `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` and `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`. The `guest` persona and the baseline reachability and CSP assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "भूमिका एक सार्वजनिक प्रलेखन साइट प्रकाशित करती है। [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml) पिन `sso.enabled` और `sso.shared` to `false`, और भूमिका जहाजों नहीं `meta/users.yml` और कोई खाता प्रावधान नहीं; [`templates/env.j2`](./templates/env.j2) केवल निर्माण सेवा को कॉन्फ़िगर करता है। [`tasks/main.yml`](./tasks/main.yml) केवल कंटेनर और प्रॉक्सी स्टैक तारों और चरणों Sphinx निर्माण संदर्भ में टूलींग। कोई खाता नहीं है और कोई खाता श्रृंखला नहीं है `biber` या `administrator` व्यक्तित्व, इसलिए [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) घोषणा `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` और `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`. A. A.A. `guest` व्यक्तित्व और बेसलाइन पहुंच क्षमता और सीएसपी दावे बिना शर्त चलाते हैं।."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role publishes a public documentation site. ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``sso.enabled`` and ``sso.shared`` to ``false``, and the role ships no ``meta/users.yml`` and no account provisioning; ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ only configures the build service. ```tasks/main.yml`` <./tasks/main.yml>`__ only wires the container and proxy stack and stages the Sphinx tooling into the build context. There is no account and no auth chain for the ``biber`` or ``administrator`` persona, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona and the baseline reachability and CSP assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "भूमिका एक सार्वजनिक प्रलेखन साइट प्रकाशित करती है। ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``sso.enabled`` and ``sso.shared`` to ``false``, and the role ships no ``meta/users.yml`` and no account provisioning; ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ only configures the build service. ```tasks/main.yml`` <./tasks/main.yml>`__ only wires the container and proxy stack and stages the Sphinx tooling into the build context. There is no account and no auth chain for the ``biber`` or ``administrator`` persona, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` व्यक्तित्व और बेसलाइन पहुंच क्षमता और सीएसपी दावे बिना शर्त चलाते हैं।."

msgid "The role reads a method with `lookup('config', application_id, 'services.<entity>.login.method.<method>.enabled')`."
msgstr ""

msgid "The role registers that Stalwart client over JMAP (``templates/jmap/oauth_client/``) as a public first-party client, with one redirect URI ``<origin>/<prefix>/oauth/callback`` and one post-logout URI ``<origin>/<prefix>/login`` per origin and URL prefix of the WebUI Application. The origins are the role’s canonical WebUI URL (``STALWART_WEBUI_BASE_URL``) in every network the node serves it on (``lookup('network_urls')``), so a Tor deployment registers its ``http://`` onion origin next to the clearnet one. Every deploy compares the registered client with that target and updates it when they differ. An origin that is no network sibling of the canonical WebUI URL MUST be added in ```templates/jmap/oauth_client/webui.json.j2`` <templates/jmap/oauth_client/webui.json.j2>`__, because a URI added in Stalwart alone is removed by the next deploy. Stalwart’s login page asks for consent for the client after the password form, so a native WebUI login shows an **Allow** step."
msgstr ""

msgid "The role registers that Stalwart client over JMAP (`templates/jmap/oauth_client/`) as a public first-party client, with one redirect URI `<origin>/<prefix>/oauth/callback` and one post-logout URI `<origin>/<prefix>/login` per origin and URL prefix of the WebUI Application. The origins are the role's canonical WebUI URL (`STALWART_WEBUI_BASE_URL`) in every network the node serves it on (`lookup('network_urls')`), so a Tor deployment registers its `http://` onion origin next to the clearnet one. Every deploy compares the registered client with that target and updates it when they differ. An origin that is no network sibling of the canonical WebUI URL MUST be added in [`templates/jmap/oauth_client/webui.json.j2`](templates/jmap/oauth_client/webui.json.j2), because a URI added in Stalwart alone is removed by the next deploy. Stalwart's login page asks for consent for the client after the password form, so a native WebUI login shows an **Allow** step."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role renders ``settings.yml`` from the deployment’s own secret key and mounts it read-only. ``formats`` carries ``json`` next to ``html``, because a machine consumer gets HTTP 403 on the JSON endpoint otherwise, and the rate limiter is off since the only clients are platform services on the container network."
msgstr "भूमिका ``settings.yml`` तैनाती की अपनी गुप्त कुंजी से और इसे केवल पढ़ने के लिए माउंट करता है। ``formats`` करना ``json`` आगे ``html``, क्योंकि एक मशीन उपभोक्ता HTTP हो जाता है 403 अन्यथा JSON समापन बिंदु पर, और दर सीमक बंद हो जाता है क्योंकि केवल ग्राहक कंटेनर नेटवर्क पर प्लेटफॉर्म सेवाएं हैं।."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The role renders `settings.yml` from the deployment's own secret key and mounts it read-only. `formats` carries `json` next to `html`, because a machine consumer gets HTTP 403 on the JSON endpoint otherwise, and the rate limiter is off since the only clients are platform services on the container network."
msgstr "भूमिका `settings.yml` तैनाती की अपनी गुप्त कुंजी से और इसे केवल पढ़ने के लिए माउंट करता है। `formats` करना `json` आगे `html`, क्योंकि एक मशीन उपभोक्ता HTTP हो जाता है 403 अन्यथा JSON समापन बिंदु पर, और दर सीमक बंद हो जाता है क्योंकि केवल ग्राहक कंटेनर नेटवर्क पर प्लेटफॉर्म सेवाएं हैं।."

msgid "The role renders the shared ``default.css`` and ``bootstrap.css`` once per deployment onto the CDN, links them with a cache-busting version, and adds the role’s own ``style.css`` and ``design.js`` when the role ships them. The role’s ``style.css`` is rendered per vhost and stored once per network the role is served on: the first network keeps ``style.css``, every further one gets ``<label>-style.css`` (for example ``onion-style.css``), and each vhost links the file of its own network. Light and dark tokens switch with ``prefers-color-scheme``; a role mirrors an app-native theme switch through ``<html data-design-theme=\"light|dark\">``."
msgstr ""

msgid "The role renders the shared `default.css` and `bootstrap.css` once per deployment onto the CDN, links them with a cache-busting version, and adds the role's own `style.css` and `design.js` when the role ships them. The role's `style.css` is rendered per vhost and stored once per network the role is served on: the first network keeps `style.css`, every further one gets `<label>-style.css` (for example `onion-style.css`), and each vhost links the file of its own network. Light and dark tokens switch with `prefers-color-scheme`; a role mirrors an app-native theme switch through `<html data-design-theme=\"light|dark\">`."
msgstr ""

msgid "The role renders the signaling ``server.conf`` from ```signaling.conf.j2`` <./templates/signaling.conf.j2>`__, ``janus.jcfg`` from ```janus.jcfg.j2`` <./templates/janus.jcfg.j2>`__ and the recording ``server.conf`` from ```recording.conf.j2`` <./templates/recording.conf.j2>`__, and the version updaters raise every pin. `docs/Administration.md <docs/Administration.md#talk-high-performance-backend>`__ describes how the services connect, how a version update reaches them and how the first deploy replaces ``nextcloud/aio-talk``."
msgstr ""

msgid "The role renders the signaling `server.conf` from [`signaling.conf.j2`](./templates/signaling.conf.j2), `janus.jcfg` from [`janus.jcfg.j2`](./templates/janus.jcfg.j2) and the recording `server.conf` from [`recording.conf.j2`](./templates/recording.conf.j2), and the version updaters raise every pin. [docs/Administration.md](docs/Administration.md#talk-high-performance-backend) describes how the services connect, how a version update reaches them and how the first deploy replaces `nextcloud/aio-talk`."
