msgid "The runnable journey lives in `files/playwright/test-login-biber.js`, which grants biber the KIX user group over the Keycloak Admin API for the scenario, drives `runKixLoginLogoutFlow` through both stages to the universal logout and removes the grant again. Its LDAP-only twin, and the one in `files/playwright/test-login-administrator.js`, sign in through the KIX-LDAP login directly while SSO is off, with biber's group membership written to the directory. `files/playwright/test-rbac.js` asserts the proxy refusal for biber without a group and, while SSO is off, the contact fields and Superuser role the sync applies. The path back to the generic persona is a KIX build that accepts the proxy's trusted headers instead of demanding its own login."
