msgid "Use these values only if the configured pool supports them. The settings ``freellmapi.alias`` and ``freellmapi.model`` select the public alias and upstream model ID; their initial values are ``freellmapi/auto`` and ``auto``. This pool is always classified as remote, even though its gateway container runs locally. The existing ``router.remote_fallback`` and privacy rules still apply. Dynamic pools are excluded from speed measurement because successive requests may use different models. Do not configure FreeLLMAPI to route back to this LiteLLM instance: that would create a forwarding cycle."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use these values only if the configured pool supports them. The settings `freellmapi.alias` and `freellmapi.model` select the public alias and upstream model ID; their initial values are `freellmapi/auto` and `auto`. This pool is always classified as remote, even though its gateway container runs locally. The existing `router.remote_fallback` and privacy rules still apply. Dynamic pools are excluded from speed measurement because successive requests may use different models. Do not configure FreeLLMAPI to route back to this LiteLLM instance: that would create a forwarding cycle."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Use this as a practical reference when you want to understand how local development is expected to work."
msgstr "इसे एक व्यावहारिक संदर्भ के रूप में उपयोग करें जब आप यह समझना चाहते हैं कि स्थानीय विकास कैसे काम करने की उम्मीद है।."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Use this for static lint checks that walk ``meta/services.yml`` text. Runtime callers should prefer ``get_sso_config``'s ``is_enabled`` predicate, which already runs against the merged + rendered payload."
msgstr "इसे स्थिर लिंट चेक के लिए उपयोग करें जो चलना है ``meta/services.yml`` पाठ रनटाइम कॉलर्स को पसंद करना चाहिए ``get_sso_config``' ``is_enabled`` भविष्यवाणी, जो पहले से ही विलय + रेंडर पेलोड के खिलाफ चलता है।."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Use this for stdout output, log messages, or any place a YAML representation is needed without an on-disk file. There is no cache involved (the destination is a string, not a path), but the helper exists so callers don't have to ``import yaml`` just to call ``yaml.safe_dump`` — keeping every YAML touchpoint in ``utils.cache.yaml``."
msgstr "इसे stdout आउटपुट, लॉग संदेश, या किसी भी स्थान के लिए उपयोग करें, एक ऑन-डिस्क फ़ाइल के बिना एक YAML प्रतिनिधित्व की आवश्यकता है। इसमें कोई कैश शामिल नहीं है (गंतव्य एक स्ट्रिंग है, एक पथ नहीं), लेकिन सहायक मौजूद है इसलिए कॉलर्स को नहीं करना पड़ता है ``import yaml`` बस कॉल करने के लिए ``yaml.safe_dump`` - प्रत्येक YAML टचपॉइंट को बनाए रखना ``utils.cache.yaml``।."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Use this guide to create inventories, run a full deploy, and redeploy an existing environment with `infinito` commands only. The audience is the operator running deploys against a managed (production or staging) host. Contributors iterating on a local development stack should follow [Local Deploy](../contributing/actions/deploy.md) instead."
msgstr "इन्वेंटरी बनाने के लिए इस गाइड का उपयोग करें, पूरी तैनाती करें और मौजूदा वातावरण को फिर से शुरू करें `infinito` केवल आदेश। दर्शक एक प्रबंधित के खिलाफ ऑपरेटर चल तैनाती है (उत्पादन या मंचन) मेजबान। स्थानीय विकास स्टैक पर iterating योगदानकर्ताओं का पालन करना चाहिए [स्थानीय तैनाती](../contributing/actions/deploy.md) इसके बजाय।."

# translated-by: libretranslate
