msgid "When `meta/variants.yml` declares variant-specific behaviour (WordPress Multisite, Moodle LDAP-only, …), the spec MAY add scenarios that gate on a variant-specific env var via `test.skip(!process.env.<VARIANT>_ENABLED, \"<reason naming the variant flag>\")`. Variant-gated scenarios MUST surface in the reporter as `skipped` with a reason naming the flag, never as silent no-ops."
msgstr "कब `meta/variants.yml` संस्करण-विशिष्ट व्यवहार घोषित (WordPress मल्टीसाइट Moodle LDAP केवल, ...), कल्पना MAY परिदृश्यों को जोड़ता है जो एक संस्करण-विशिष्ट env var के माध्यम से गेट करता है `test.skip(!process.env.<VARIANT>_ENABLED, \"<reason naming the variant flag>\")`. रिपोर्टर में वैरिएंट-गेटेड परिदृश्य MUST सतह के रूप में `skipped` एक कारण से ध्वज नाम देने के साथ, कभी भी चुप नहीं है।."

msgid "When `services.talk.enabled` is true, Nextcloud Talk uses the dedicated `web-svc-coturn` service for STUN and TURN. `web-app-nextcloud` runs no TURN server of its own."
msgstr ""

msgid "When `svc-net-tor` is among the deployed applications, the inventory build mints the node onion offline: [tor_node.py](../../cli/administration/inventory/provision/tor_node.py) calls `cli.administration.inventory.onion`, which writes `hostname`, `hs_ed25519_public_key` and `hs_ed25519_secret_key` to `.onion-identity/hs/` at the root of the checkout that deploys, and the build writes the address into `applications.svc-net-tor.services.tor.node` of the host's `host_vars`. A later build reuses the files, so the address does not change. To mint or print the address without a build, run from the checkout root:"
msgstr ""

msgid "When `svc-net-tor` is deployed, the node runs in the `multi` network mode by default: every role with a Tor bond keeps its clearnet domains and gains one `<sub>.<node>.onion` sibling per domain, each served by its own vhost. `NETWORK_MODE: tor` serves those roles on onion only (see [network_modes.md](../../docs/contributing/design/network_modes.md)). The Tor daemon runs as a host-network compose sidecar and maps one hidden service to the host OpenResty (`HiddenServicePort 80 -> <backend host>:80`, where the backend host `TOR_HS_BACKEND_HOST` is the docker bridge address in compose, `127.0.0.1` when there is none, and the node's default IPv4 address in swarm); per-app subdomains (`<app>.<node>.onion`) are routed by the `Host` header. Onion vhosts serve plain HTTP (onion v3 already provides transport encryption and server authentication), so apps behind them receive `X-Forwarded-Proto: http`."
msgstr ""

