msgid "`services.freellmapi.startup_config` accepts the upstream declarative startup configuration as a mapping. It can declare provider `keys`, `customProviders` such as LM Studio, `models`, `fallback`, and `routing`. Entries with credentials belong in the encrypted inventory. The role always passes it as `FREEAPI_CONFIG_JSON`, adding the central platform administrator under `admin`. An inventory-supplied `startup_config.admin` cannot override this identity. The rendered environment contains the administrator password and must retain the framework's credential-file protections. Upstream still ignores `admin` on already initialized installations; the post-start reconciliation is what handles credential changes on redeploy."
msgstr ""

msgid "`services.keycloak.admin.allowed_networks` limits every path under `/admin`, which carries the admin console and the admin REST API under `/admin/realms`, to the listed source networks. Each entry is an IPv4 or IPv6 address or a CIDR block. The vhost renders one `allow` per entry followed by `deny all`, so any other client gets `403`. The list ships empty, and an empty list leaves `/admin` open. Declare it in the inventory:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`services.keycloak.email.policy` in [services.yml](meta/services.yml) decides which address a user's primary one is."
msgstr ""

msgid "`services.keycloak.realm` in [services.yml](meta/services.yml) decides how the application realm offers one-time passwords. A fresh realm imports these values and every deploy converges an existing realm to them."
msgstr ""

msgid "`services.keycloak_adapter.enabled` defaults to false: the `TOKEN_AUTH_URL` hand-off to the adapter, the `token_affiliation` split between moderators and named members, and the `X-Forwarded-Proto` rewrite of `files/keycloak_adapter/forwarded_scheme.ts` on an onion vhost are not yet proven on `stable-11031` (upstream tested `stable-10532-1` with its own `body.html` and `meet.conf`, which this role does not ship); options: flip the default to `\"{{ 'web-app-keycloak' in group_names }}\"` once variant 0 passes `test-keycloak-adapter.js` and a two-browser conference test with a moderator and a non-moderator realm user."
msgstr ""

